      "role": "user",
      "content": "1.3 is a much more comfortable number for the committee. Thanks for digging into that. \n\nJust to be absolutely clear for the audit and compliance folder: does this 1.3 ratio account for the total indebtedness that the bank is actually exposed to? I want to make sure that when we're performing the final due diligence, there aren't any massive subsidiary-level liabilities that would surfaced later and make it look like we ignored them in this initial assessment. Can you confirm this figure is as comprehensive as possible for our risk reporting?",
